From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shital Shah <2096835+sytelus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:53:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] allocator: shm allocator for backends without DRM

CShmAllocator hands out CPU buffers (XRGB/ARGB8888, packed stride) backed by a memfd, or by a file in
a given directory so another process can map the same memory (e.g. a viewer outside the VM). Files
are sized with fallocate (ftruncate fallback), rounded up to whole pages (some shared filesystems,
e.g. WSLg's DAX share, reject other sizes), mapped MAP_SHARED, and pre-faulted by writing every
page once (MAP_POPULATE would only read-fault a shared mapping; on DAX the first write to a page is
several hundred times slower than later ones).
The swapchain falls back to the shm format when a buffer has no dmabuf.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
